    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive output today rests heavily on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, whose 65.86 score marks him as our primary anchor. Despite his \"Lineup Pending\" status, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Casey Legumina\u2019s 4.32 xERA; the combination of a park factor boost and his projected #3 spot in the order maximizes his run-production potential. Following him is **Drake Baldwin**, whose 59.14 score is buoyed by his premium position at the top of the order against Hart. While the matchup is neutral, **Drake Baldwin** earns a significant 10% bump for his leadoff duties, ensuring he gets the most plate appearances to contribute to our scarcity-driven categories.\n\nConversely, we are forced to treat **Brayan Rocchio** (44.53) and **Dominic Smith** (40.67) as marginal plays. **Brayan Rocchio** suffers from the SP skill of Bradley, T, and while his order placement mitigates some downside, he remains on the lower end of our active threshold. **Dominic Smith** presents the most risk today, as the L/L platoon disadvantage against Hart severely compresses his ceiling. While our high-upside speed threats like **Nasim Nunez**, **Cole Carrigg**, and **Luis Lara** remain on the bench or in the pipeline, the current daily roster construction favors the higher floor of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Drake Baldwin** over the situational volatility of our reserve depth. We are closely monitoring the status of **Jackson Merrill**, whose absence from the lineup continues to leave a void in our outfield production, forcing us to lean on the current active quartet until the rest of our core\u2014including **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014returns to action.",
